  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 528ecde27feefd74eb359b784c14f552, type: 3}
  m_Name: Anna
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DollConfig
  dollName: Anna
  dollOwner: Wendy Kobayashi, 11 y.o., female, deceased
  dollStory: Wendy always loved playing with Anna. One night, when Wendy's parents
    weren't home, she was left alone. Tragically, when her parents returned, they
    found Wendy had bled to death from a head wound caused by one of her other toys.
    The lights weren't working, and her room was in complete disarray, with toys
    scattered everywhere. According to the police investigation, the ceiling light,
    Wendy's lamp, and her phone's flashlight all stopped working at around the same
    time. Since it was already dark outside, her room was left in pitch-black darkness.
    It's possible that Wendy became frightened and tried to escape but tripped and
    fell on a sharp object. However, the cause of the sudden blackout remains unknown.
  dollReason: Anna harbors a dangerous spirit that is sensitive to light. It was
    confirmed that she was the cause of the blackout within a 30-yard radius. The
    scattered toys were merely the result of Wendy's untidiness, which ultimately
    led to her tripping over them in a panic and falling onto a sharp wooden tree
    sculpture. Wendy died from blood loss 42 minutes later. Her parents discovered
    her body two hours later when they returned from their anniversary date. The
    doll cannot be trusted with children anymore.
